Changes: converted from the original 44.1 kHz stereo WAV to raw 8-bit
signed PCM at 8192 Hz, mono and stereo.

PSG music for mml(1) (/dev/psg)
===============================

jacques.mml     "Frere Jacques" (traditional, public domain) as a
                three-part round with a noise drum, arranged for this
                port; it uses all four PSG channels.

minuet.mml      Minuet in G major, BWV Anh. 114, from the Notebook for
                Anna Magdalena Bach (now attributed to Christian
                Petzold; public domain): the melody, the melody an
                octave lower and a simple bass, about 26 seconds.

grace.mml       "Amazing Grace" (the tune "New Britain", 1829; public
                domain): the melody with a vibrato and a portamento, a
                pad gliding between the chords and a bass, about 29
                seconds.

All three arrangements were written for this port from the music itself, not
taken from other MML files, and are under this tree's license.

	mml /usr/share/examples/gba/jacques.mml
	mml /usr/share/examples/gba/minuet.mml
	mml /usr/share/examples/gba/grace.mml

Playing it while a PCM sample plays on /dev/audio shows the GBA mixing
the two.
